# Avoid em dashes

Do not write em dashes in prose. Rewrite them into a comma, parentheses, a colon, or a second
sentence. Swapping the dash for a semicolon keeps the same habit in different clothes.

Data dashes stay untouched: empty-cell placeholders in tables, bibliography separators, dashes
inside a cited title, dashes in URLs and file names, and site or page titles such as
`Silício — Chip Making`.
